# P8 · Scale and specialty features · Week 52 onward · R8 Ongoing
# exit: 1 per feature: adoption target agreed before build
# nfr:  1 each feature gated by its own evidence review
# pkg:  1 minor-version release notes
# dep:  1 regulatory classification review for any decision-support feature

@epic MDV-P8-E01 | Demand-driven features | P8-01, P8-02, P8-03, P8-04, P8-05, P8-06 | Features released individually as minor versions when demand and evidence justify them.

=== MDV-P8-001
title: Feature intake: adoption target, evidence review and regulatory classification check for every P8 feature
type: Chore
epic: MDV-P8-E01
prd: P8-01, P8-02, P8-03, P8-04, P8-05, P8-06
covers: exit:1, nfr:1, dep:1, pkg:1
priority: MUST
roles: Founder, Clinical advisor
labels: governance
estimate: 1
weeks: 52
confidence: 85 | Process requirement is explicit.
sources: PRD v2 P8
desc:
Before building any P8 feature: agreed adoption target, evidence review (customer demand, clinical evidence), regulatory classification review for any decision-support aspect, and a minor-version release-notes template.
ac:
- Each P8 ticket links an approved intake record before work starts.
- Minor-version release notes template exists and is used.

=== MDV-P8-002
title: Teleconsultation: video visit with identity check and ambient notes (A-11)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E01
prd: P8-01
screens: A-11
priority: SHOULD
roles: Doctor, Patient
labels: telehealth, video
estimate: 6
weeks: 52-56
depends: MDV-P8-001, MDV-P3-012
confidence: 60 | Hi-fi design exists; telemedicine rules per country and video vendor to decide (open decision: earlier only if two paying clinics require it).
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (A-11 Teleconsultation); PRD v2 open decision "Teleconsultation earlier than P8?"
desc:
Video visit (ACS video) with identity check of the patient, camera/mic/recording toggles, consent for recording, ambient notes through the P3 pipeline, portal join flow.
ac:
- Identity check is completed and recorded before consultation starts.
- Recording requires its own consent; declined → manual note.
- Telemedicine guideline requirements per country are documented and met.

=== MDV-P8-003
title: Vaccinations and recalls: child, travel and adult schedules with reminders (E-08)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E01
prd: P8-02
screens: E-08
priority: COULD
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: vaccinations
estimate: 4
weeks: 54-57
depends: MDV-P8-001
confidence: 70 | Hi-fi E-08 exists (schedule vs given, dose recording); clinical scope approval required.
sources: design/Medvya Clinical Screens (E-08)
desc:
Schedule vs given (age, vaccines, date, status Given / Reported by guardian / Due / Upcoming), record dose given (vaccine, batch/lot, expiry, site & route, given by, next due), recall reminders.
ac:
- Only if clinically approved for scope (intake record).
- Dose records capture batch, expiry, site/route and giver; next due computed per schedule.
- Recall reminders respect consent and contain no clinical details.

=== MDV-P8-004
title: India ABDM: ABHA consent requests and linked records from other facilities
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E01
prd: P8-03
priority: SHOULD
roles: Doctor, Patient
labels: abdm, india, interop
estimate: 6
weeks: 56-60
depends: MDV-P8-001
confidence: 45 | Requires ABDM sandbox certification and current implementation-guide conformance.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (India ABHA consent-based records); docs/03-architecture/integrations.md
desc:
HIP/HIU integration: Scan & Share at reception, consent requests approved on the patient's phone, linked records (FHIR bundles) shown with source for the consented period; care-context linking of Medvya visits.
ac:
- ABDM sandbox certification passed.
- Linked records display with ABDM provenance and consent period, never merged into verified data without clinician acceptance.

