=== MDV-P8-006
title: Front-desk extras: kiosk/QR self check-in, clinic letter inbox, offline read and draft (N-16)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E01
prd: P8-05
screens: N-16
priority: COULD
roles: Patient, Receptionist, Doctor
labels: kiosk, offline, design-needed
estimate: 6
weeks: 58-62
depends: MDV-P8-001
confidence: 45 | DESIGN NEEDED; offline mode has significant security implications.
sources: design/Medvya Gap Analysis (kiosk, letter inbox, offline LATER); PRD v2 P8-05
desc:
Self check-in on tablet/QR (confirm details and consent), dedicated clinic email inbox with auto-matching and "needs filing" queue, offline read of today's charts and draft notes with encrypted local storage and sync.
ac:
- Designs approved before build.
- Offline data is encrypted, time-limited and wiped on sign-out; conflicts on sync are surfaced.
- Inbound letters are matched with the same identity-match rules as results.

=== MDV-P8-007
title: Platform: public FHIR APIs, native mobile apps (Expo), saved migration templates per vendor, specialty templates
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E01
prd: P8-06
priority: COULD
roles: Developer, Partners
labels: platform, mobile, api
estimate: 8
weeks: 60-64
depends: MDV-P8-001, MDV-P5-019
confidence: 45 | Broad bucket; each item needs its own intake.
sources: PRD v2 P8-06; design/Medvya Build Plan (mobile phase 2 with Expo)
desc:
Public FHIR APIs with SMART-on-FHIR auth, native apps (Expo) sharing contracts and i18n, a library of saved migration templates per legacy vendor, and additional specialty note templates.
ac:
- Each item passes its own intake record before work starts.
- Public APIs enforce the same tenant/relationship/purpose authorisation and audit.
